From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maicon Alves <alvesmaiconn@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 13:18:12 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 32/44] client: digging paced as in Minecraft

The next node could be dug after the last one's dig time divided by the
crack animation's frames, at most 0.3 s and 0.15 s after an instant one:
0.03 s with a fast pick on stone, so a tunnel went by two or three times
faster than in Minecraft. Minecraft waits 5 ticks, 0.25 s, after every
block, in survival and creative alike; so does this now (repeat_dig_time
still sets a longer minimum).

Minecraft digs five times slower off the ground (jumping, flying, on a
ladder) and five times slower again with the eyes in water. The dig time
now runs at that pace, from the moment the player leaves the ground or
puts the head under water, as Minecraft adds its progress tick by tick.
Water is a node of the group water at the eye position.

The hand's capabilities are used when they dig faster than the wielded
item's, not only when the item can't dig: in Minecraft's creative mode a
block breaks at once whatever is held, and a creative hand that does
that is otherwise unused while a tool is in hand. The server's dig check
does the same, so it doesn't count those digs as too fast. In survival
the hand never wins with the handheld's Minecraft capabilities, where
every tool digs a block at least as fast as the hand.

Checked in the native build with a steel pick held on a stone wall:
0.656 s from block to block (Minecraft 0.40 + 0.25); flying, 2.23 s
(2.0 + 0.25); in creative with the pick, 0.25 to 0.29 s.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/client/game.cpp b/src/client/game.cpp
index 63f23c58a..36faeaa6a 100644
--- a/src/client/game.cpp
+++ b/src/client/game.cpp
@@ -3402,11 +3402,11 @@ void Game::handleDigging(const PointedThing &pointed, const v3s16 &nodepos,
 			&tool_item.getToolCapabilities(itemdef_manager, &hand_item),
 			tool_item.wear);
 
-	// If can't dig, try hand
-	if (!params.diggable) {
-		params = getDigParams(features.groups,
-				&hand_item.getToolCapabilities(itemdef_manager));
-	}
+	// If can't dig, or the hand digs faster (a creative hand), use the hand
+	const DigParams hand_params = getDigParams(features.groups,
+			&hand_item.getToolCapabilities(itemdef_manager));
+	if (!params.diggable || (hand_params.diggable && hand_params.time < params.time))
+		params = hand_params;
 
 	if (!params.diggable) {
 		// I guess nobody will wait for this long
@@ -3467,15 +3467,8 @@ void Game::handleDigging(const PointedThing &pointed, const v3s16 &nodepos,
 		if (g_settings->getBool("safe_dig_and_place"))
 			runData.digging_blocked = true;
 
-		runData.nodig_delay_timer =
-				runData.dig_time_complete / (float)crack_animation_length;
-
-		// We don't want a corresponding delay to very time consuming nodes
-		// and nodes without digging time (e.g. torches) get a fixed delay.
-		if (runData.nodig_delay_timer > 0.3f)
-			runData.nodig_delay_timer = 0.3f;
-		else if (runData.dig_instantly)
-			runData.nodig_delay_timer = 0.15f;
+		// As in Minecraft, the next node is dug 0.25 s (5 ticks) after one breaks
+		runData.nodig_delay_timer = 0.25f;
 
 		// Ensure that the delay between breaking nodes
 		// (dig_time_complete + nodig_delay_timer) is at least the
@@ -3509,7 +3502,12 @@ void Game::handleDigging(const PointedThing &pointed, const v3s16 &nodepos,
 	}
 
 	if (runData.dig_time_complete < 100000.0) {
-		runData.dig_time += dtime;
+		// As in Minecraft, five times slower off the ground and five times slower with the head in water
+		f32 slowdown = player->touching_ground ? 1.0f : 5.0f;
+		const MapNode eye = map.getNode(floatToInt(player->getEyePosition(), BS));
+		if (itemgroup_get(nodedef_manager->get(eye).groups, "water") > 0)
+			slowdown *= 5.0f;
+		runData.dig_time += dtime / slowdown;
 	} else {
 		runData.dig_time = 0;
 		client->setCrack(-1, nodepos);
